{#
The "pl" mark, geometry and nothing else — every colourway is a LogoStyle and
every renderer of the mark goes through this macro, so the letters cannot
drift between the topbar, the settings tiles and the favicon.

The shape, for whoever tunes it next (each fix was a reviewed round):
  - both letters start on one top line (y=7) and end on one bottom line
    (y=42): the p's stem descends to exactly where the l's tail rests;
  - the p's bowl ends high (y≈26) so the head reads square-ish, not tall;
  - the l runs straight down to y=37 before its tail turns on a tight radius
    — turned earlier, the column of ink under the l stopped visibly higher
    than the p's and the p read as deeper, bounding boxes notwithstanding;
  - the ink spans x 10.25–46.75 / y 4.25–44.75 raw, so the translate centres
    the DRAWING in the 48-frame; without it every icon tile leaned right.

Seven strokes, and their draw order is a contract: LogoStyle::strokes()
returns paints for exactly this sequence, and the sweeps are built on it —
reorder the strokes and every gradient breaks silently.

`data-logo-stroke` carries the index so the appearance page can repaint a
mark live when a style is picked, without knowing the geometry. Only marks
rendered with `live` opt into that repaint: the settings tiles each preview
their OWN style and must not be painted over by the choice they offer.
#}
{% macro mark(style, size, dark = false, live = false) %}
    {% set c = style.strokes(dark) %}
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 48 48" width="{{ size }}" height="{{ size }}" aria-hidden="true" data-logo-mark{% if live %} data-logo-live{% endif %}>
        <g transform="translate(-4.5 -0.5)" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="5.5">
            <line x1="13" y1="11" x2="13" y2="42" stroke="{{ c[0] }}" data-logo-stroke="0"/>
            <path d="M13 11 Q13 7 17 7 L23 7 Q29 7 29 13" stroke="{{ c[1] }}" data-logo-stroke="1"/>
            <line x1="29" y1="13" x2="29" y2="22" stroke="{{ c[2] }}" data-logo-stroke="2"/>
            <path d="M29 22 Q29 26 23 26 L17 26 Q13 26 13 22" stroke="{{ c[3] }}" data-logo-stroke="3"/>
            <line x1="37" y1="7" x2="37" y2="26" stroke="{{ c[4] }}" data-logo-stroke="4"/>
            <line x1="37" y1="26" x2="37" y2="37" stroke="{{ c[5] }}" data-logo-stroke="5"/>
            <path d="M37 37 Q37 42 42 42 L44 42" stroke="{{ c[6] }}" data-logo-stroke="6"/>
        </g>
    </svg>
{% endmacro %}
